---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const guide = 'https://github.com/izyuumi/yorozu/blob/projectx/docs/setup.md';
---
<Base title="Yorozu — A native chat app for your OpenClaw agent" description="Yorozu is a native iPhone, iPad and Mac app for chatting with your own OpenClaw agent, end-to-end encrypted through a relay that cannot read your messages.">
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <meta property="og:title" content="Yorozu">
    <meta property="og:description" content="A native chat app for your own OpenClaw agent, on iPhone, iPad and Mac. End-to-end encrypted.">
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://yorozu.yumi.to/">
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://yorozu.yumi.to/assets/icon.png">
  </Fragment>
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="title">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <h1 id="title">Your OpenClaw agent.<br><em>In your pocket.</em></h1>
        <p class="lede">Yorozu <span class="kana" lang="ja">(よろず)</span> is a native chat app for the <a href="https://docs.openclaw.ai/install">OpenClaw</a> agent you already run. Its plugin makes Yorozu a channel of your Gateway, like Signal or Telegram, and the app on your iPhone, iPad or Mac talks to it end-to-end encrypted. OpenClaw runs the agent, its memory and its schedules; Yorozu carries the conversation.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button" href="/iphone">Get Yorozu on the App Store</a>
          <a class="button ghost" href="/mac">Download for Mac</a>
          <a class="button ghost" href={guide}>Set up the plugin</a>
        </div>
        <p class="fine">Yorozu 0.9 · iPhone and iPad: iOS 18+ · Mac: macOS 15+ · Needs your own OpenClaw Gateway · <a href="https://github.com/izyuumi/yorozu">Open source, MIT</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <style>
    /* The hero is copy only. Astro emits this as an external stylesheet
       (inlineStylesheets: 'never'), which the CSP allows. */
    .hero-inner { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
    .hero-copy { padding-bottom: clamp(48px, 8vw, 110px); }
  </style>

  <section class="more" aria-labelledby="chat-title">
    <h2 id="chat-title">Every conversation, on every device.</h2>
    <dl class="facts">
      <div><dt>Many conversations</dt><dd>Start a new conversation with +. Each one is its own OpenClaw session, listed on every paired device, with full history loaded from your Gateway.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>See the work</dt><dd>Replies arrive whole, with a typing indicator while the agent runs and each tool call shown as a collapsed row.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Delivery and read marks</dt><dd>Every message goes from Sent to Delivered to Read. Read state and unread badges stay in step across your devices.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Rename, archive, delete</dt><dd>Titles are made for you after the first turn. Rename, archive or delete from any device and the others follow.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="more" aria-labelledby="more-title">
    <h2 id="more-title">Built for the agent you already run.</h2>
    <dl class="facts">
      <div><dt>Automations</dt><dd>See your agent's scheduled jobs with their next run, and change one with Edit in Chat: the agent edits it with its own tools. A job can deliver its result into a conversation.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Files, both ways</dt><dd>Send photos, camera shots and files, or share them from other apps. Files the agent returns open in the conversation.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Notifications</dt><dd>One push per finished reply, with a preview only your device can open. Nothing is pushed for the conversation you are looking at.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>A native app</dt><dd>SwiftUI on iPhone, iPad and Mac, with light, dark or system appearance and an accent colour of your choice.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="relay" aria-labelledby="relay-title">
    <h2 id="relay-title">The relay can't read a word of it.</h2>
    <figure class="diagram" role="img" aria-label="Your devices and your OpenClaw Gateway exchange messages encrypted with ChaCha20-Poly1305 through a relay that sees only size and timing.">
      <span class="diagram-art" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <figcaption aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="diagram-encryption">ChaCha20-Poly1305 · End-to-end encrypted</span>
        <span class="diagram-labels"><span>iPhone</span><span class="diagram-relay">sees size and timing</span><span>Gateway</span></span>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <dl class="facts">
      <div><dt>Fresh keys for every connection</dt><dd>Each connection runs a Noise IK handshake. Private keys stay in the device Keychain and in your Gateway's credentials store.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>No open port</dt><dd>The plugin connects out to the relay, so the computer running your Gateway needs no port forwarding.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Send while it sleeps</dt><dd>While your Gateway is offline, the relay holds what your devices send for up to 24 hours, sealed, and hands it over when the Gateway is back.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>No Yorozu account</dt><dd>No email, no password, no analytics. Your model providers and their logins stay in OpenClaw.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="iphone-availability" id="get" aria-labelledby="get-title">
    <div class="availability-intro">
      <h2 id="get-title">Get Yorozu.</h2>
      <p>Yorozu has two parts: the plugin in your OpenClaw Gateway, and the app on each device.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="installation-options">
      <article>
        <h3>The plugin</h3>
        <p>Install the Yorozu channel plugin in your OpenClaw Gateway (OpenClaw 2026.9.8 or later). The <a href={guide}>setup guide</a> has the commands and settings.</p>
        <a href={guide}>Open the setup guide</a>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>iPhone and iPad</h3>
        <p>Yorozu is on the App Store for iPhone and iPad with iOS 18 or later. No Gateway yet? Enter <code>YOROZU-DEMO</code> on the pairing screen to look around with sample conversations.</p>
        <a href="/iphone">Get Yorozu on the App Store</a>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Mac</h3>
        <p>The same app runs natively on Macs with macOS 15 or later. Move it to Applications and open it; it updates itself.</p>
        <a href="/mac">Download for Mac</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="steps" id="pair" aria-labelledby="steps-title">
    <h2 id="steps-title">Then pair once.</h2>
    <p class="steps-intro">You'll need <a href="https://docs.openclaw.ai/install">OpenClaw</a> running with the Yorozu plugin. Keep the Gateway's computer awake and online to reach your agent.</p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
        <h3>Make a pairing code</h3>
        <p>On the computer that runs your Gateway, run <code>openclaw yorozu pair</code>. It prints a QR code and a link that work once and expire after 10 minutes.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
        <h3>Pair your device</h3>
        <p>Scan the QR with the Camera or in Yorozu, or paste the link. Check that the fingerprint matches the one the command printed. No Yorozu account needed.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
        <h3>Talk from anywhere</h3>
        <p>Your conversations live in OpenClaw. Every paired device sees them all, through the relay.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="warning" id="before-you-install" aria-labelledby="risk-title">
    <h2 id="risk-title">Before you install</h2>
    <p><strong>Your agent acts with the accounts you give OpenClaw.</strong> If OpenClaw drives Claude Code, Codex or a model through a subscription login, Anthropic and OpenAI decide what use of that subscription is allowed, change those rules without notice, and have suspended accounts used with third-party agent tools. For the lowest risk, use an API key rather than a subscription login.</p>
    <p>AI agents take real actions: they run commands, edit and delete files and can send messages. Review what your agent is allowed to do. See the <a href="/terms/">Terms of Use</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
